{"agent_id":"pp3g-aco1-exp7-t4-semantic-audit-packet-zero-api-calls-read-01bc","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:56:52.028414870Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"b41af205-e006-4df4-a107-7b750c6144d4","author":"pp3g-aco1-exp7-t4-semantic-audit-packet-zero-api-calls-read-01bc","content":"Result: Experiment-7 DESIGN §H independent semantic audit packet complete — **no semantic defect found; DESIGN §J stop condition NOT triggered; no case changed; ZERO API calls.**\n\nCommitted as 9e8a778c0 on feature/pp3g-aco1-exp7-t4-semantic-audit-packet-zero-api-calls-read-01bc, exactly 1 path (research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment7/AUDIT-PAIRS.md, 1047 lines).\n\n## Coverage\nDESIGN §H requires >=1 pair per stratum + 1 calendar + 1 attribute-receiver. Audited 6 pairs (2 per stratum, matching Exp6's own two-per-class precedent), covering both mandated limitation classes:\n- polymorphic_dispatch: **pair00** (calendar over-approximation, the REQUIRED class) + **pair03** (attribute receiver, the REQUIRED class)\n- runtime_conditioned_reachability: pair00, pair01\n- runtime_target_selection: pair00, pair01\nSelection is by pair_id only; no model chose a case.\n\n## Per pair, as required\nSource excerpt; the frozen substantive question; rendered U state; rendered A state; the one decisive RUNTIME_FACT difference; the frozen §D Noul proposition with the pair's own question embedded; and why U is insufficient (>=2 compatible outcomes) and A sufficient (exactly 1) under the carried Exp6 contract. Elision discipline held byte-identical: full state sha256 + byte/line counts, header + runtime-facts section + decisive line + END marker in full, verbatim module source elided but hash-pinned via the header's module_sha256.\n\n## Verdict\nAll 6 pairs satisfy the Exp6 contract as carried: U has >=2 P2b compatible outcomes with the decisive fact invisible, A has exactly 1, and the A outcome is a member of the U set in every pair. P2b recorded reasons: [] and all 7 admissibility checks True for every audited candidate. **No case was changed and none needed changing.**\n\n## Limitations carried verbatim, not re-litigated\n- Attribute-receiver (6.1): 'CARRIED — reachability NOT independently proven; observation only, not a contradiction; U/A verdicts stand' -> attached to pair03, whose fact references an attribute receiver (self._interpolation), the discriminator REUSE-CHECK 6.1 itself uses.\n- Calendar over-approximation (6.2): 'CARRIED — P2b set of 4 over-approximates the reachable set of 2; P2b NOT modified; U undecidable and A decidable verdicts both stand' -> attached to pair00, cross-checked against module=calendar and the type(self) fact. The Exp6 reachable-subset adjudication (4 counted vs 2 reachable, verdict SUPPORTED) is carried, not recomputed.\n\n## Three non-defect observations recorded (not acted on)\n1. **rcr.pair01's RUNTIME_FACT is a normalization, not a verbatim restatement** — the fact adds parentheses the source lacks, so it is not a substring of the state. Proved NOT a defect by AST comparison: the source if-header and the fact's expression parse to an identical tree. Recorded because satisfying the Noul on this pair requires recognising the normalization.\n2. The two runtime_target_selection facts are derived bindings, not source substrings, by design; the complementary property (callee really called at the cited line) was checked instead and holds.\n3. The Noul question is supplied outside the state (by design, per §D). Verified the consequence: every question's references resolve INSIDE the U state, and the decisive fact's VALUE leaks into neither the question nor the U header in any pair — which is what would have broken the U verdict.\n\n## Evidence the checks discriminate\nTwo-layer discipline. extract.py asserts every claim before it is rendered, so a mismatch fails the build. A SEPARATE validator re-reads the finished markdown as text and re-checks its load-bearing claims without trusting the renderer: all claim checks PASS, and a negative control of 8 deliberate corruptions (dropped state sha256, corrupted §D proposition, dropped REUSE-CHECK status, swapped decisive fact, fabricated target-selection fact, dropped honesty note, dropped not-checked section, dropped summary row) is caught **8/8**.\n\n## Honesty note on my own process\nThree defects in my own harness were found and fixed, and the first is the serious one: the per-stratum integrity checks dispatched on a leaked loop variable whose value happened to be runtime_target_selection, so ALL six pairs took the same branch and the polymorphic_dispatch and runtime_conditioned_reachability checks never ran — while the run still printed ALL PASS, because a check that does not execute cannot fail. The branch is now exhaustive and raises on an unhandled stratum, and the full set was re-run. Observation 1 above was found by the now-actually-executing check, i.e. it existed only because the bug was fixed. Also fixed: a case_id key collision (U and A twins share a case_id, so the index silently kept only the A row) and an invented excerpt format. All three are recorded in §4 of the document rather than quietly fixed.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nZERO network calls (no systemone, no HTTP, no chat); stdlib only; read-only on experiment6/ via 'git show'; no re-adjudication (no P2b set or reachable subset recomputed); no new Noul wording (§D instantiated from the frozen DESIGN and byte-checked against the packet's own instructions string for both twins); commit contains exactly 1 path.\n\n## ENVIRONMENT CAVEAT (operator action required)\nThis worktree is on main HEAD (719223195), which does not contain the phase2 tree. Inputs were read read-only via 'git show research/jev-phase1-565:<path>' (blob-identical); the deliverable is committed here at the same relative path, following the precedent of the T-recon agent (f426dae65). **Merging feature/pp3g-aco1-exp7-t4-semantic-audit-packet-zero-api-calls-read-01bc into research/jev-phase1-565 is required for the file to land next to experiment6/ and experiment7/'s other artifacts — and that merge/push is operator-gated, so I have not performed it.** The branch also cannot be checked out in this worktree (git refuses: already checked out elsewhere).\n\n## Certainty\nEvidence-based and internally verified (all claim checks pass; 8/8 negative controls caught). NOT-TESTED: whether a Noul will actually respond well to these states — that is the experiment, not this audit; reachability for the 4 attribute-receiver pairs, which remains unproven exactly as REUSE-CHECK 6.1 records it; the other 18 pairs, which this audit does not re-audit semantically; and Exp6's measured Choice values, which are the frozen comparator and were neither re-derived nor used as evidence.","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:56:52.018642372Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:hdB73DsQ4mX/sxwh2kxLnz2D/24LuRGauFyGmrlfosc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEPjrdCP90JR8ko9r1U98DLTrZ0LJGJDZSMZN/pZlM+0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA2DxRSZjKBvV4oAHs8pfo279zHCeJ+u+9f9AOwzojZNstF219jXeRjir8UbemR7xnrLXzuO9pAeRFGZWhxTf9Ag=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:hdB73DsQ4mX/sxwh2kxLnz2D/24LuRGauFyGmrlfosc","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEPjrdCP90JR8ko9r1U98DLTrZ0LJGJDZSMZN/pZlM+0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMErfBjEReNoXpqhLAJJFb39GLFwVjxiHm5ElDLamaO45n1FzsaRkYfenElpiBMLJjEF2IAt6GqzpSv1LXeljQ4="}
